# Claude Code runtime data — never commit
#
# NOTE: .claude/skills/* is ignored wholesale; every skill that should sync
# MUST have a `!.claude/skills/<name>` exception below, or `chezmoi add`
# silently skips it. See README "Adding a new skill".
#
# CI enforces this both ways (.github/scripts/check-skill-exceptions.sh): every
# dot_claude/skills/<name>/ must have managed FILES in `chezmoi managed`, and
# every exception line must have a matching source dir. Counting files, not just
# the directory entry, is deliberate: a `.claude/skills/<name>/**` rule anywhere
# below re-ignores the contents while chezmoi goes on listing the directory, so
# the skill would sync nothing and still look managed.
# Do not "simplify" this file —
# dropping an exception here is invisible locally and only shows up as a skill
# that quietly stopped syncing to the other Mac.
.claude/cache
.claude/sessions
.claude/history.jsonl
.claude/stats-cache.json
.claude/telemetry
.claude/tasks
.claude/todos
.claude/plans
.claude/debug
.claude/paste-cache
.claude/image-cache
.claude/shell-snapshots
.claude/session-env
.claude/ide
.claude/plugins
.claude/file-history
.claude/backups
.claude/projects
.claude/skills/*
!.claude/skills/linear-crud
!.claude/skills/todo
!.claude/skills/session-audit
!.claude/skills/backlog-groom
.claude/worktrees
.claude/settings.json.bak
.claude/settings.local.json

# Repo documentation — belongs in the repo, not deployed into $HOME.
# Without these, chezmoi treats them as target files and writes ~/README.md and
# ~/SETUP.md (it did, for months).
README.md
SETUP.md
docs

# CI config — repo-only. These document intent; they are NOT a second line of
# defence. They name the DOTTED targets, and chezmoi skipping dot-prefixed
# source entries is why those targets never exist in the first place. Rename
# .ruff.toml to ruff.toml and the target becomes `ruff.toml`, which matches
# nothing here and lands in $HOME — measured, not assumed.
# check-no-ci-config-in-home.sh is the actual guard.
.ruff.toml
.gitleaks.toml
.github

# Secrets — never commit
.env
.env.*
*.secret

# Repo documentation for humans and reviewers — not deployed into $HOME.
docs
